## 0. Mathematical Foundations — Statistics and Analysis

File: [`Spqr/Math/Gf.lean`](../../Spqr/Math/Gf.lean) (360 lines)

This file provides the basic mathematical knowledge required to verify
all GF(2¹⁶) functions. Every spec file in `Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Gf/`
depends (directly or transitively) on the definitions and lemmas below.

### 0a. Core Definitions

| Definition | Type | Description |
|------------|------|-------------|
| `GF216` | `abbrev` | `GaloisField 2 16` — the abstract finite field with 2¹⁶ elements (from Mathlib). |
| `natToGF2Poly` | `Nat → (ZMod 2)[X]` | Interprets a natural number's binary representation as a GF(2) polynomial. Bit `i` of `n` becomes the coefficient of `Xⁱ`. |
| `POLY_GF2` | `(ZMod 2)[X]` | The irreducible polynomial `X¹⁶ + X¹² + X³ + X + 1` (= `0x1100b`). Defines `GF(2¹⁶) ≅ (ZMod 2)[X] / (POLY_GF2)`. |
| `φ` | `(ZMod 2)[X] →+* GF216` | A chosen ring homomorphism factoring through the quotient; `φ POLY_GF2 = 0`. |
| `Nat.toGF216` | `Nat → GF216` | Composite `φ ∘ natToGF2Poly`: interprets a `u16` value as an element of `GF(2¹⁶)`. |

### 0b. Lemmas and Theorems (Verified — No `sorry`)

| Lemma/Theorem | Status | What It States |
|---------------|--------|----------------|
| `natToGF2Poly_coeff` | ✅ | Coefficient of `natToGF2Poly n` at position `m` is `1` iff bit `m` of `n` is set. |
| `natToGF2Poly_zero` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly 0 = 0`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_xor` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly (a ^^^ b) = natToGF2Poly a + natToGF2Poly b` (XOR = polynomial addition). |
| `natToGF2Poly_shiftLeft` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly (a <<< k) = natToGF2Poly a * X^k` (shift = multiply by `X^k`). |
| `natToGF2Poly_POLY` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly 0x1100b = POLY_GF2`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_mod_eq_of_lt` | ✅ | If `v < 2^n`, then `natToGF2Poly (v % 2^n) = natToGF2Poly v`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_split` | ✅ | Decomposes `natToGF2Poly v` into lower-`n`-bit and upper parts. |
| `natToGF2Poly_inj` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly` is injective (equal polynomials ⇒ equal bit patterns). |
| `POLY_GF2_monic` | ✅ | `POLY_GF2` is monic (leading coeff = 1). |
| `POLY_GF2_natDegree` | ✅ | `POLY_GF2.natDegree = 16`. |
| `zmod2_poly_neg_eq` | ✅ | In `(ZMod 2)[X]`, `-a = a` (char 2). |
| `zmod2_poly_sub_eq_add` | ✅ | In `(ZMod 2)[X]`, `a - b = a + b` (char 2). |
| `POLY_GF2_dvd_modByMonic_sub` | ✅ | `POLY_GF2 ∣ (p %ₘ POLY_GF2 - p)`. |
| `modByMonic_modByMonic_self` | ✅ | `(p %ₘ POLY_GF2) %ₘ POLY_GF2 = p %ₘ POLY_GF2` (idempotence). |
| `ringHom_modByMonic` | ✅ | If `φ P = 0`, then `φ (p %ₘ P) = φ p` (transport along quotient). |
| `natToGF2Poly_modByMonic_eq` | ✅ | Multiplicativity of `%ₘ POLY_GF2` (quotient ring multiplication). |
| `exists_ringHom_modByMonic` | ✅ | Existence of `φ : (ZMod 2)[X] →+* GF216` with `φ POLY_GF2 = 0`. |
| `hφ` | ✅ | The chosen `φ` satisfies `φ POLY_GF2 = 0`. |

### 0c. Known `sorry` in Math Foundations

| Theorem | Location | Status | Explanation |
|---------|----------|--------|-------------|
| `POLY_GF2_irreducible` | `Spqr/Math/Gf.lean:204` | ⚠️ `sorry` | States that `POLY_GF2 = X¹⁶ + X¹² + X³ + X + 1` is irreducible over `ZMod 2`. This is a true and well-known fact, but Lean 4 / Mathlib does not yet provide a `Decidable (Irreducible p)` instance for `(ZMod q)[X]`, so `native_decide` cannot be used. Proving it manually requires either building a decidability instance or exhibiting a primitive root — both non-trivial. This `sorry` is used only in `exists_ringHom_modByMonic` (to construct `φ`) and does **not** affect any of the 19 verified function specs, which work at the `Nat`/bitwise level rather than the abstract `GF216` level. |

